  "implementation": [
    "private managed resource state carries an exact numeric count of committed borrowing frames",
    "frame roots the borrowed wrapper and private owner-state array; native metadata holds only slot indices",
    "aliases within one frame share one lease; separate frames release independently",
    "borrow leases prevent dispose and owned lowering/commit until native frame retirement",
    "all transfer, liveness and counter-cap checks finish before any ownership mutation",
    "state is rooted before lower can grow the frame array; canonical handle is already a native scalar",
    "Promise init hooks and context capture complete before import_begin commits staged ownership and borrows",
    "commit failure returns zero without publishing SuspendedImport; runtime releases the failed frame rather than leaking it to C",
    "generated async import starts canonical I/O only after successful begin; removes the later unchecked commit",
    "cancellation or Promise settlement alone does not release native borrow storage; C-owned failed frames release leases when retired after acknowledgement",
    "frame Drop retires loans through private rooted slots without validating the current registry or invoking JS",
    "dead managed anchor skips all managed loan access at heap teardown; poisoned slot metadata test exercises this path"
  ],
